{"reference":"2 Chronicles 15","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":15,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A recurring pattern","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One way to read verses 1–15 is as part of a recurring pattern in Judah’s reigns: seeking the LORD, turning to him in distress, and receiving prophetic instruction stand opposite abandoning him. In this chapter, Azariah’s message gives Asa’s reforms and the people’s covenant their interpretive frame.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 15:1-15"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_015_0fd60a405f6b52fc0ff9d584"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}